---
// The install page. Its whole job is to hand one line to the person so their AI does the work,
// and the instructions the AI reads are a plain file at /install.md, not this page: a page is
// for a person, a file is what an agent can fetch and follow. Once the hosted pilot opens
// (src/lib/hosted.ts), the page's head offers the hosted inbox and its button, and the line for
// your AI follows as the other way. The closed lede keeps its line breaks as they were, so the
// closed page is built exactly as before. After the line for your AI and what it does come the three
// ways to run it by hand (SELF_HOST): one command on a server, the Docker image on a platform,
// Cloudflare Workers.
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { DEPLOY_URL, HOSTED_INSTALL } from "../lib/hosted";
import { WOO_NOTICE } from "../lib/integrations";
import { SELF_HOST } from "../lib/self-host";

const PROMPT =
  "Install Surfing Dog Inbox for my business. Follow the instructions at https://surfingdog.ai/install.md exactly, ask me before anything that costs money or changes DNS, and verify each step before moving on.";
const CONNECT_PROMPT =
  "Connect my Surfing Dog Inbox to the software I already use. Follow https://surfingdog.ai/connect.md exactly, ask me which tools I use, ask before changing a setting in another system or sending an email for me, and test every connection before telling me it works.";
---

<Layout
  title="Install an inbox for AI bookings in one line · Surfing Dog"
  description="Tell your AI to install it. One line, and the instructions it needs are written for it, step by step, with a check after each one."
  image="/art/og-inbox-v1.png"
>
  <section class="wrap wrap-read section is-head" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-h">
    <p class="eyebrow">Install</p>
    <h1 class="h-page" id="install-h">{HOSTED_INSTALL?.title ?? "Let your AI do it"}</h1>
    {
      HOSTED_INSTALL ? (
        <>
          <p class="lede">{HOSTED_INSTALL.lede}</p>
          <p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href={HOSTED_INSTALL.cta.href}>
              {HOSTED_INSTALL.cta.label}
            </a>
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
    <p class="lede">
      You do not have to read any of this. Give the line below to Claude, ChatGPT, Codex, Grok or whatever you use,
      and it will set the whole thing up: the server, your subdomain, email in, and your first sign-in.
    </p>
      )
    }
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="prompt-h">
    <div class="wrap wrap-read">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">{HOSTED_INSTALL?.promptEyebrow ?? "Step one, and often the only step"}</p>
          <h2 class="h-section" id="prompt-h">Paste this to your AI</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <pre class="glass panel prompt"><code>{PROMPT}</code></pre>
      <p class="hint">
        It will ask you a few things it cannot know: where you want it to run, which subdomain, which address signs in
        as the owner. It is told to ask before anything that costs money or touches your DNS, and to check its work
        after every step rather than assume.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="what-h" data-reveal>
    <div class="wrap wrap-read">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What it does</p>
          <h2 class="h-section" id="what-h">The same five things, either way</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><b>Puts it somewhere.</b> Your Cloudflare account, free to start, or your own server.</li>
        <li><b>Gives it your subdomain.</b> Usually <code>inbox.yourdomain.com</code>, with a certificate.</li>
        <li><b>Turns on email in,</b> so a customer can simply write to it, and proves it with a test message.</li>
        <li><b>Signs you in</b> and hands you the key, once.</li>
        <li><b>Sets your business up:</b> hours, services, products, and the rules that answer for you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="hint">
        The instructions it follows are at <a class="link" href="/install.md">/install.md</a>. They are written for a
        machine: every secret is generated rather than guessed, every step has a command that proves it worked, and it
        is told to stop and tell you rather than carry on when a check fails. Read them yourself if you like.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="yourself" aria-labelledby="yourself-h">
    <div class="wrap wrap-read">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Or by hand</p>
          <h2 class="h-section" id="yourself-h">Three ways</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ol class="run-ways" data-reveal="stagger">
        {
          SELF_HOST.map((way) => (
            <li class="run-way" id={way.id}>
              <h3 class="way-name">{way.name}</h3>
              <p class="way-what">{way.what}</p>
              {way.command ? (
                <div class="way-cmd">
                  <code>{way.command}</code>
                  <button class="way-copy" type="button" data-copy={way.command} aria-label={`Copy: ${way.name}`} hidden>
                    Copy
                  </button>
                </div>
              ) : (
                <p>
                  <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" href={DEPLOY_URL} rel="noopener">
                    Deploy to Cloudflare
                  </a>
                </p>
              )}
              <p class="way-links">
                {way.links.map((link, i) => (
                  <>
                    {i > 0 && <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>}
                    <a class="link" href={link.href}>
                      {link.label}
                    </a>
                  </>
                ))}
              </p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="connect-h" id="connect" data-reveal>
    <div class="wrap wrap-read">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Already running other software?</p>
          <h2 class="h-section" id="connect-h">Connect what you already use</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">
        Your shop, your calendar, your CRM: you do not need a plug-in for each. Give your AI the line below. It connects
        the inbox to them where that works today, and tells you plainly where it does not.
      </p>
      <pre class="glass panel prompt"><code>{CONNECT_PROMPT}</code></pre>
      <p class="hint">
        Each system that calls your inbox gets its own key, which you can revoke in Settings → Keys. The steps it
        follows are at
        <a class="link" href="/connect.md">/connect.md</a>. Calendars, Calendly, payments, shops (WooCommerce®, Shopify,
        Square), property systems, ordering systems and job tools connect in Settings → Integrations today
        (<a class="link" href="/docs/integrations/">which, and how</a>). Missing yours? Vote for it on
        <a class="link" href="/requests/">the requests board</a>. {WOO_NOTICE}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<script>
  import { wireCopyButtons } from "../lib/copy";
  wireCopyButtons(".run-way [data-copy]");
</script>

<style>
  .run-ways {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .run-way {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
    padding: var(--sp-5) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .way-name {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-ui);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .way-what,
  .way-links {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--fs-fine);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .way-cmd {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
    padding: 8px 8px 8px 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-control);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground) 40%, transparent);
  }
  .way-cmd code {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
    padding-top: 3px;
    font-size: var(--fs-mono);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    user-select: all;
  }
  .way-copy {
    flex: none;
    height: 26px;
    padding: 0 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: transparent;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--fs-fine);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .way-copy:hover,
  .way-copy:focus-visible {
    background: var(--pill-bg-hover);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .prompt {
    padding: var(--sp-5);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    font-size: var(--fs-mono);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .panel code {
    font-size: var(--fs-mono);
  }
</style>
